      }

**The redeemDeposit() function allows the owner of a deposit to redeem/withdraw it if the deposit status is STATUS_FAILED. It loops through the deposit's tokens and amounts, clears the balances from the Port contract for each one, and deletes the deposit info.**

**However, it does not check if a partial redemption has already occurred. For example:**

**- Deposit is created with 2 tokens, 10 of token A and 20 of token B.**
**- Deposit fails, status set to STATUS_FAILED.**
**- Attacker calls redeemDeposit(), redeems 10 of token A.**
**- Deposit info still exists with 20 of token B remaining.**
**- Attacker can call redeemDeposit() again to redeem the 20 of token B.**

**So the attacker was able to redeem the deposit twice for a total of 30 tokens, instead of the original 20.**

