# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The premature state change allows assets to be withdrawn before the final settlement result is known, which can lead to loss of assets or asset duplication across chains.

## Proof of Concept
**The key points are:**
**• retrieveSettlement allows the settlement owner to retrieve their deposited assets back to the root chain if the settlement fails on the destination chain.**
**• It sets settlement.owner = address(0) to mark the settlement as retrieved.**
**• However, this doesn't guarantee the settlement actually failed and assets were returned. The destination chain could still successfully complete the settlement later.**
**• So assets could be retrieved on root chain and also minted on destination chain, leading to a double spend.**

