# Vulnerability details

## Impact
_bridgeOut function should burn hTokens inside it when underlying tokens and hTokens are bridged out. However _bridgeOut function in ArbitrumRootBranchPort doesn't burn them instead transfer them to the address of RootPort. This may affect the price of hTokens negatively because it doesn't reduce their total supply.

## Proof of Concept
In BranchPort, _bridgeOut function burns tokens correctly between the lines 531 and 533 as shown below.

```
if(_hTokenAmount > 0) {
         _localAddress.safeTransferFrom(_depositor,address(this),_hTokenAmount);
         ERC20hTokenBranch(_localAddress).burn(_hTokenAmount);}
```

However _bridgeOut function in ArbitrumRootBranchPort overrides it and shadows burn functionality with calling 
bridgeToRootFromLocalBranch(...) function.

```
 function _bridgeOut(
        address _depositor,
        address _localAddress,
        address _underlyingAddress,
        uint256 _amount,
        uint256 _deposit
    ) internal override {
        //Store Underlying Tokens
        if (_deposit > 0) {
            _underlyingAddress.safeTransferFrom(_depositor, address(this), _deposit);
        }

        //Burn hTokens if any are being used
        if (_amount - _deposit > 0) {
            unchecked {
                IRootPort(rootPortAddress).bridgeToRootFromLocalBranch(_depositor, _localAddress, _amount - _deposit);
            }
        }
    }
```


bridgeToRootFromLocalBranch which is implemented in RootPort only transfers hTokens to RootPort as following line in RootPort demonstrates: 

 ```
function bridgeToRootFromLocalBranch(address _from, address _hToken, uint256 _amount)
        external
        override
        requiresLocalBranchPort
    {
        if (!isGlobalAddress[_hToken]) revert UnrecognizedToken();

        _hToken.safeTransferFrom(_from, address(this), _amount);
    }
```

