# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Function ``payableCall`` within contract ``VirtualAccount.sol`` does not have any access control and can be invoked by anyone. This function can be invoked without sending any ETH (i.e. msg.value = 0) so it will effectively behave as function ``call``. That way, the access control stablished by modifier ``requiresApprovedCaller`` in function ``call`` is bypassed.
By using ``payableCall``, an attacker can drain all of a user's funds.

