The vulnerability in the code of [VirtualAccount.sol at line 85](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-09-maia/blob/main/src/VirtualAccount.sol#L85) The `payableCall` functions are not protected against reentrancy attacks. The potential for reentrancy exists, especially if there are state-changing operations in this contract or linked contracts that could be affected by the calls made in this function.

To protect against reentrancy attacks, you can use a modifier. Here's a simple implementation:

## Proof of Concept

```solidity
