## Impact

As I understand it, `hToken` appears to be a type of token used to represent native assets from multiple different chains in a single liquidity management environment. This allows native assets to remain locked in their specific chains while still having the ability to provide liquidity and profit from activity on multiple different chains.

If `_recipient` is an invalid address or has no value, the `bridgeToRoot` function can still perform the transfer, resulting in a loss of funds in your system.

If there is a large loss of funds due to sending hTokens to invalid addresses, users may lose trust in your system and service. This can affect your reputation and passive customers.

